{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftexplain\/kernelshaptheory"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain\/KernelSHAPTheory","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"metadata":{"title":"Game-Theoretic Interpretability with Kernel SHAP","role":"collectionGroup","roleHeading":"API Collection","modules":[{"name":"SwiftExplain"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain"]]},"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Compute exact and sampled Shapley feature attributions to explain predictions of any machine learning model."}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"SHAP-Explainer-APIs","title":"SHAP Explainer APIs","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain\/KernelSHAP"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"SHAP (SHapley Additive exPlanations)","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is a game-theoretic approach to explain the output of any machine learning model. It connects optimal credit allocation with local explanations using the classic Shapley values from cooperative game theory."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"1-The-Four-Shapley-Axioms","level":2,"text":"1. The Four Shapley Axioms"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Shapley values are the only attribution method that uniquely satisfies all four fundamental properties:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Efficiency","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Feature attributions sum up to the difference between model prediction "},{"code":"f(x)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and expected background prediction "},{"code":"E[f(X)]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"Note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Σ_i=1..M φ_i = f(x) - E[f(X)]","type":"codeVoice"}]}],"type":"aside","style":"note"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Symmetry","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":": If two features contribute equally to all possible feature subsets, their attributions are equal."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Dummy (Null Player)","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":": A feature that does not change the model prediction for any coalition receives an attribution of zero ("},{"code":"φ_i = 0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Additivity","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":": For ensemble models "},{"code":"f = f1 + f2","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", attributions satisfy "},{"code":"φ_i(f) = φ_i(f1) + φ_i(f2)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"2-Explaining-Predictions-in-SwiftSci","level":2,"text":"2. Explaining Predictions in SwiftSci"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import SwiftExplain","import SwiftML","","\/\/ Initialize KernelSHAP with background dataset","let explainer = try KernelSHAP(","    model: { features in","        \/\/ Arbitrary inference closure","        return try await rf.predictProba(features: features).map { $0[1] }","    },","    background: backgroundSamples,","    nSamples: 100",")","","\/\/ Compute Shapley values for an instance","let instance = [35.0, 75000.0, 720.0, 1.0]","let explanation = try await explainer.explain(instance: instance)","","print(\"Base Value: \\(explanation.baseValue)\")","print(\"Feature Attributions: \\(explanation.values)\")"]}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://SwiftExplain/documentation/SwiftExplain/KernelSHAP":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Model interpretation using the KernelSHAP algorithm."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"KernelSHAP","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"actor","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"KernelSHAP","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain\/KernelSHAP","title":"KernelSHAP","type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swiftexplain\/kernelshap"},"doc://SwiftExplain/documentation/SwiftExplain":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiftexplain","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain","abstract":[{"text":"Model Explainability, SHAP & Feature Attributions.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"collection","title":"SwiftExplain"}}}